# onnxruntime-node's postinstall fetches a CUDA execution provider from nuget.org
# on Linux: 272 MB of native library that this app never loads (it runs on the
# CPU and WebGPU providers bundled in the package) and that scripts/after-pack.mjs
# strips out of every artifact anyway.
#
# package.json's `allowScripts` already blocks that postinstall, but it pins an
# exact version: the first install here bumped onnxruntime-node past the pinned
# entry, stopped covering it, and pulled the 272 MB down without a word. This
# setting does not depend on the version, so a future bump cannot quietly undo
# it — and it keeps `npm install` talking to nothing but the registry.
#
# npm calls this an "Unknown project config" because it is the package's own
# option rather than one of npm's. It is still passed through as
# npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install, which is what the install script reads —
# verified by allowing the script and watching it skip the download anyway.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
